{
  "workflow": {
    "description": "Workflow B for the work instance (issue #462), proven headless with stubs: the same shape as workflow-b with the work agents only. A test author on the work Claude agent (claude-work) writes failing tests from the ticket, one writer on Codex (a different family) implements until they pass, then build, tests, lint and the coverage gate each run through the gate shim. One critic worker on claude-work (a different family from the Codex writer) reviews the change and the finding check keeps only findings with a checkable quote. A round with an actionable finding sends the ticket back to the Codex writer, at most twice, in fixed nodes (repair-1, repair-2), so no loop exists. Every Codex node (the writer and both repairs) is preceded by a grant-check node that reserves one Codex node start against the run's grant; when the grant is missing or used up its failure edge leads to the grant-refused manual check, so the run pauses before Codex. After the second failed repair an Opus escalation node on claude-work judges the ticket and a manual check pauses the run for the owner. No gate node has a failure edge, so a failing gate ends the run in failure.",
    "version": "0.1",
    "id": "workflow-b-work",
    "entry": "test-author",
    "control": {
      "max_attempts": 1,
      "max_rounds": 1
    },
    "nodes": [
      {
        "type": "worker",
        "id": "test-author",
        "executionSlotId": "slot-test-author",
        "provider": "claude-work",
        "model": "sonnet",
        "profile": "pf-builtin-dev",
        "goal": "You are the test author, on the work Claude agent, a different family from the Codex writer. Read the ticket's acceptance criteria in the requirement document and write failing tests for them, one test per criterion, in the repository's own test style. Write tests only: no implementation, no change to any non-test file. Answer with one fenced json block holding ok and nothing else.",
        "output": {
          "kind": "json",
          "artifact": "tests-written",
          "schema": {
            "ok": true
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "worker",
        "id": "grant-check-writer",
        "executionSlotId": "slot-grant-check-writer",
        "provider": "grant-writer",
        "model": "stub-model",
        "profile": "pf-builtin-dev",
        "goal": "Run the pinned gold-band-run-start grant-check wrapper for the Codex node writer (--node writer) and answer with the report it wrote as one fenced json block and nothing else. The wrapper reserves one Codex node start against this run's grant and refuses when there is none.",
        "output": {
          "kind": "json",
          "artifact": "grant-check-writer-report",
          "schema": {
            "run_id": "string",
            "attempt": 1,
            "command": "string",
            "exit_code": 0,
            "output_hash": "string",
            "timestamp": "string"
          }
        },
        "success_condition": {
          "path": "$.exit_code",
          "equals": 0
        }
      },
